[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2588413924","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2588413924","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2588413924,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aSA_k","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-13T23:05:55Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T17:47:45Z","body":"For posterity, these are the matrices:\r\n\r\n**Edit:** I've removed a number of the matrices from this comment that were used to generate the matrices used in this PR because they were not that great. I got them from Blender's OCIO files, but using this tool gives better results: https://www.colour-science.org:8010/apps/rgb_colourspace_transformation_matrix\r\n\r\nBlender AgX inset:\r\n0.856627153315983 0.137318972929847 0.11189821299995\r\n0.0951212405381588 0.761241990602591 0.0767994186031903\r\n0.0482516061458583 0.101439036467562 0.811302368396859\r\n\r\nBlender AgX outset:\r\n\r\n0.899796955911611 0.11142098895748 0.11142098895748\r\n0.0871996192028351 0.875575586156966 0.0871996192028349\r\n0.013003424885555 0.0130034248855548 0.801379391839686\r\n\r\nBlender AgX outset inverse:\r\n1.1271005818144366432 -0.14132976349843826565 -0.14132976349843824772\r\n-0.1106066430966032116 1.1578237022162717623 -0.11060664309660291788\r\n-0.016493938717834568157 -0.01649393871783425265 1.2519364065950402828","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2588413924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2588822186","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2588822186","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2588822186,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aTkqq","user":{"login":"EaryChow","id":59176246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MTc2MjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59176246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow","html_url":"https://github.com/EaryChow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T03:10:15Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T03:11:03Z","body":"I don't know how far ahead Godot has planned in terms of color, but we chose to use Rec.2020 as AgX's formation space was because we believe Blender will one day fix the remaining color management issue and move on to a wider gamut rendering space for the PBR engines to work in. This means when the time comes, the light transport renderer will natively generate out-of-rec.709-gamut values. The decision to use Rec.2020 was for future proofing. Please consider the future of Godot, are you sure Godot will stay not having color management system forever?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2588822186/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589856329","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2589856329","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2589856329,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aXhJJ","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T13:01:53Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T13:03:20Z","body":"> Please consider the future of Godot, are you sure Godot will stay not having color management system forever?\n\nRegardless of this, the implementation of how non-sRGB input will be passed to the tone mapping functions is not yet known. This PR does not preclude handling other colour spaces in the future. All tone mapping, including AgX, will likely need to be reworked (if only for performance reasons) to support other color spaces.\n\nIf we knew exactly how we were going to handle other colour spaces in the future, then we could design with that in mind, but right now it's impossible, and honestly a bad idea, to try and take a guess at how that might unfold in the future. Because these decisions and the code is well documented, it will be easy to adjust AgX when it comes time.\n\nA \"Custom tone mapping\" feature definitely needs to be added to the engine. This will allow users to have more bespoke tone mapping functionality, including LUT support so the Blender AgX LUT can be used without much modification. For the built-in features of a general purpose game engine, it's very important that performance is not sacrificed for a relatively few number of users.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589856329/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589875288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2589875288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2589875288,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aXlxY","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T13:10:53Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T13:15:47Z","body":"I also want to clarify to others who looking at this PR that all AgX transformations and calculations are still performed in rec 2020 space, just like in Blender.\n\nThe only difference is how negative RGB inputs to the tone mapper are clipped. In many games, there are no negative RGB inputs at all, so this PR makes literally zero difference besides improving performance. The only common cases where a visual difference might be seen is in some very vibrant HDR image files (and only in the Forward+ renderer) and negative lights.\n\nPlease post here if you know of other common scenarios that would result in negative RGB values that should be clipped in color space other than sRGB.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589875288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589893009","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2589893009","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2589893009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aXqGR","user":{"login":"EaryChow","id":59176246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MTc2MjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59176246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow","html_url":"https://github.com/EaryChow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EaryChow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T13:19:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T13:34:48Z","body":"> If we knew exactly how we were going to handle other colour spaces in the future, then we could design with that in mind, but right now it's impossible, and honestly a bad idea, to try and take a guess at how that might unfold in the future.\r\n\r\nIn general, a good idea is to leave room for a configurable color management system like OCIO in the future, when the time comes, your biggest enemy is \"hardcoded sRGB assumptions scattered everywhere accross the entire software throughout the years\", and by \"remaining color management issues Blender needs to fix\", I meant \"histroical sRGB hardcoded assumptions in many parts of the Blender\". For instance Blender's texture paint and video sequencer is still having weird color management issues that nobody really knows what is going on.\r\n\r\nOnce OCIO is supported, the Linear RGB rendering space that the light transport PBR engine renders in, can be configured by modifying 1 single line in a txt file. But then you would see a lot of the parts in the software are still assuming the sRGB working space because the devs back then assumed sRGB and thought it was a good idea for \"optimization\". For instance, Blender's Blackbody emission was hardcoded to clip to the Rec.709 gamut boundry (quite similar to what you are trying to do) before I reported it, and it's since then fixed by having the Blackbody chromaticity data re-generated and dynamically clipped to the current configurable working space.\r\n\r\nI just feel the need to warn, if hardcoding sRGB asumption is still a good idea to you then feel free. \r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589893009/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590027585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2590027585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2590027585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aYK9B","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T14:12:34Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T14:12:34Z","body":"Yes, balancing maintainable code for the future of other colour spaces and performance today on low-spec mobile devices is definitely an important consideration.\n\nThanks for your thoughts! ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590027585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2602819311","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101515#issuecomment-2602819311","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101515","id":2602819311,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bI97v","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-20T16:17:13Z","updated_at":"2025-01-20T16:17:13Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2602819311/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]